    "result_text": "I've made the change: in the invoice breakdown, each discount's line now shows what it takes off as a negative amount, e.g. **-$30.00**. The acceptance test passes under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What changed:** only one cell in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/invoices/invoice-detail.ts`, plus its header comment. That cell is the amount column of the line each discount already had. It now holds a new `breakdown-discount-row-{id}` element (the one the test checks). That element shows a minus sign followed by the amount.\n\n**Kept as it was:** the existing `discount-row-amount` anchor still exists and still shows the positive amount (\"$30.00\"). It just moved from the table cell to an inner element with the same text. I did this so tests that read the old value don't break, since the project rules don't allow renaming or removing existing anchors.\n\n**No migration or server change:** the server already sends how much each discount takes off, and the per-discount lines already existed. Only their sign needed changing. The task brief said \"OfficeFloor server\", but this app's server is actually Spring Boot (OfficeFloor is just the package name).\n\n**Left positive:** the \"Discount\" / \"Combined discount\" summary row below the per-discount lines still shows its total as a positive number. If you want that one shown as negative too, it's a one-line change. I left it because it's the total of the lines above rather than a line of its own.",
